cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  IndicGEO Study 01: Same question, different brands. English versus Hinglish
  buying prompts across ChatGPT, Gemini, and Perplexity in India
message: >-
  If you use this dataset or its findings, please cite it as below. Source code
  in this repository is MIT licensed; the dataset, reports, and documentation
  are licensed CC BY 4.0. The license field below records the code license;
  see LICENSE-DATA for the dataset licensing scope.
type: dataset
version: 1.1.0
date-released: '2026-10-14'
license: MIT
repository-code: 'https://github.com/ifham001/IndicGEO'
url: 'https://depra.ai'
authors:
  - name: Depra Research
    website: 'https://depra.ai'
    email: team@depra.ai
abstract: >-
  A controlled comparison of English and Hinglish (romanized Hindi-English
  code-mix) purchase-intent prompts against three production AI answer engines,
  geolocated to India. Ten brand-unaided buying prompts across skincare and
  fashion, each written as an independently reviewed semantically equivalent
  English/Hinglish pair, were run eight times per language against ChatGPT,
  Gemini, and Perplexity in a single 57-minute window, yielding 480 responses
  with complete raw API payloads. Using each engine's own rerun-to-rerun
  variability as the null baseline, prompt language measurably changes the set
  of brands recommended and the set of sources cited, with effect sizes
  spanning an order of magnitude across engines: ChatGPT is approximately
  language-invariant, Gemini is moderately sensitive and attaches citations to
  90 percent of English answers but only 41 percent of Hinglish answers, and
  Perplexity is strongly sensitive. The repository publishes the frozen prompt
  set, all raw responses, the brand lexicon, the analysis code, and the
  verification logs so that every reported number can be recomputed. Version
  1.1.0 adds the October 2026 re-run of the identical design (479 responses)
  with a wave-to-wave comparison, lexicon sensitivity check, stability
  spot-check and three independent recomputations.
keywords:
  - generative engine optimization
  - GEO
  - AEO
  - AI search
  - answer engines
  - Hinglish
  - code-mixing
  - India
  - LLM evaluation
  - brand visibility
  - multilingual NLP
  - citation analysis
